conversation, pinned current requests, and attention-required visibility in one surface while persisting valid user responses into durable history.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:18:Support multi-turn process conversation, keep unresolved current requests visible and distinct from routine progress, persist accepted user responses into history, and prevent false waiting or partial-submit states.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:26:- Distinction between routine progress and attention-required current requests\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:27:- Durable history for accepted user responses\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:28:- Rejection of invalid responses without partial visible history\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:29:- Same-session state updates after successful response submission\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:46:**AC-3.1:** During process stages that support discussion or clarification, the work surface supports multi-turn back-and-forth between the user and the process.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:57:**AC-3.2:** When the process is waiting on a specific question, decision, or clarification, the outstanding request remains visible until it is addressed or superseded.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:63:- **TC-3.2b: Outstanding request clears or changes after response**\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:66:  - Then: The outstanding request clears or is replaced by the new current request\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:68:**AC-3.3:** A submitted user response becomes part of durable process history for that process and remains visible when the user reloads or returns later.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:70:- **TC-3.3a: Submitted response appears in process history**\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:71:  - Given: User submits a response in a process work surface\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:73:  - Then: The response appears in that process's visible history\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:75:  - Given: User previously submitted a response in a process\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:77:  - Then: The response still appears in that process's visible history\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:79:**AC-3.4:** When the current process state does not accept a user response, the surface shows the current next action or blocking state rather than presenting the process as waiting for a reply.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:90:**AC-3.5:** An invalid process response is rejected without creating a new visible history item for that process.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:92:- **TC-3.5a: Empty response is rejected**\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:93:  - Given: User is in a process stage that accepts a response\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:94:  - When: User submits an empty or invalid response\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:95:  - Then: The response is rejected and no new visible history item is created\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:96:- **TC-3.5b: Failed response submission does not create partial history**\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:97:  - Given: User submits a response in a process stage that accepts a response\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:101:**AC-3.6:** After a successful process response submission, the submitted response and resulting process state update appear in the same session without requiring manual refresh.\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:103:- **TC-3.6a: Successful response appears in visible history in same session**\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:104:  - Given: User submits a valid response in a process stage that accepts a response\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:106:  - Then: The submitted response appears in visible history in the same session without requiring manual refresh\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/03-conversation-and-current-request.md:107:- **TC-3.6b: Resulting current r