e read them from durable source state |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:152:| A8 | Detaching a source attachment removes it from current active use but does not erase prior process history or prior durable code-update visibility | Validated | Product + Platform | Current work and prior provenance remain distinct concerns |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:179:provenance.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:207:  is the normalized GitHub identity used for uniqueness and provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:402:In Epic 6, source provenance is durable, process-specific, and complements the\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:403:artifact-version provenance aligned in Epic 5. Epic 6 requires durable\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:404:process-specific provenance records; the exact schema is deferred to Tech\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:409:Epic 6 records provenance durably at two moments:\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:411:- `informed_work` provenance is recorded when process work uses attached sources\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:413:- `received_code_update` provenance is recorded when a durable code update lands\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:416:Provenance remains durable after detach because each provenance entry copies\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:422:Each provenance relationship resolves independently. If one provenance lookup\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:423:cannot fully enrich current attachment context, the provenance endpoint still\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:426:that provenance record.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:433:- **TC-4.1a: Informing source provenance visible**\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:435:  - When: User views current source provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:437:- **TC-4.1b: Empty provenance state shown for process with no recorded source use**\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:438:  - Given: A process has no recorded source provenance yet\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:439:  - When: User views current source provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:440:  - Then: The platform shows a clear empty provenance state\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:445:- **TC-4.2a: Receiving source provenance visible**\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:447:  - When: User views current source provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:455:  - When: User views source provenance after code work\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:458:**AC-4.4:** One failing provenance lookup does not fail the rest of the\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:459:provenance surface.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:461:- **TC-4.4a: One degraded provenance entry does not hide healthy entries**\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:462:  - Given: A process has multiple provenance relationships and one cannot fully\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:464:  - When: User loads process source provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:465:  - Then: The healthy provenance entries remain visible and the failing one is\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:467:- **TC-4.4b: Degraded provenance entry falls back to durable identity**\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:468:  - Given: One provenance lookup cannot enrich current attachment metadata\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:469:  - When: The provenance surface loads\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:486:identity needed for provenance.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:491:4. System preserves prior visible provenance and prior process history\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:513:provenance or prior process history that already referenced that source.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:515:- **TC-5.2a: Prior provenance remains after detach**\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:518:  - Then: Prior visible provenance and prior process history remain available\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:588:| `/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Process work surface showing current sources for that process, including process-scoped sources and applicable project-scoped sources after shadowing/conflict rules, plus source provenance |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:604:| Get process source provenance | GET | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/source-provenance` | Returns process-specific provenance entries for attached sources that informed or received work, complementing artifact-version provenance from Epic 5; one degraded provenance lookup does not fail the whole read |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:612:| repositoryFullName | string | no | `owner/name` format when present | Normalized canonical GitHub identity used for uniqueness and provenance; may be provided by the client or derived from `repositoryUrl` during validation |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:641:| repositoryFullName | string | yes | `owner/name` format, non-empty | Normalized canonical GitHub identity used for uniqueness, conflict handling, and provenance; new in Epic 6 |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:662:| provenanceId | string | yes | non-empty | Stable provenance identifier |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:663:| sourceAttachmentId | string | no | non-empty when present | Attached source this provenance entry refers to, when the source attachment is still available |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:664:| relationshipKind | enum | yes | `informed_work` or `received_code_update` | How this source relates to the process work |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:666:| repositoryUrl | string | yes | full GitHub URL, non-empty | Operational source URL copied at the time provenance is recorded |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:668:| entryStatus | enum | yes | `ready` or `degraded` | Whether this provenance entry resolved cleanly or is returned with bounded degradation |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:669:| degradationReason | string | no | non-empty when present | Why this provenance entry is degraded when `entryStatus` is `degraded` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:670:| recordedAt | string | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Time this provenance relationship was recorded |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:672:These entries complement the artifact version provenance defined in Epic 5.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:707:| entries | array of Source Provenance Entry | yes | present | Process-specific provenance entries for attached sources that informed or received work |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:711:A successful provenance read may contain both `ready` and `degraded` entries.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:712:Per-entry provenance degradation does not force a request-level error when the\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:713:rest of the provenance surface is still readable.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:751:  references, and review/package provenance rules\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:791:- Detaching a source does not erase prior visible provenance or prior process\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:795:- One degraded provenance lookup does not fail the rest of the provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:824:   source attachments, including canonical repository identity and provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:834:5. What exact provenance surface should show informed-work relationships and\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:836:   artifact-version provenance from Epic 5?\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:844:   provenance visibility while excluding detached attachments from current\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:852:this epic owns artifact-model migration or review/package provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:858:repository identity contracts, provenance shapes, error classes, hydration and\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:859:freshness fixtures for the four-state model, Epic 5-aligned material/provenance\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:897:### Story 4: Provenance and Canonical Source Visibility\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:900:received process work, and the provenance surface degrades one failing lookup\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:905:- AC-4.1 (informing source provenance visible)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:906:- AC-4.2 (receiving source provenance visible)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:908:- AC-4.4 (one failing provenance lookup degrades independently)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:914:**Prerequisite:** Story 4\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/epic.md:918:- AC-5.2 (prior provenance remains after detach)\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:17:| AC-2.2 | TC-2.2a, TC-2.2b | Story 2 | `convex/artifacts.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | Version provenance remains visible across histories |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:23:| AC-4.1 | TC-4.1a, TC-4.1b | Story 4 | `convex/packageSnapshots.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/package-review-panel.test.ts` | Mixed-producer package publication within one project |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:24:| AC-4.2 | TC-4.2a, TC-4.2b, TC-4.2c | Story 4 | `convex/packageSnapshots.test.ts`; `convex/processPackageContexts.test.ts` | Current package-building context rule |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:25:| AC-4.3 | TC-4.3a, TC-4.3b | Story 4 | `tests/service/server/package-review-api.test.ts` | Package member pin stability |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:26:| AC-4.4 | TC-4.4a, TC-4.4b | Story 4 | `tests/service/server/package-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/review-export-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/package-review-panel.test.ts` | Mixed-producer package review and export |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:38:| Path 1.3 | Persist a later-process revision as a new version with visible provenance and updated latest-version summary | Story 2 | TC-2.1a, TC-2.2a, TC-2.3a | `convex/artifacts.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:41:| Path 2.1 | Seed a current package-building context from current refs and earlier pinned versions | Story 4 | TC-4.2a, TC-4.2c | `convex/processPackageContexts.test.ts` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:42:| Path 2.2 | Publish one mixed-producer package from valid same-project current context | Story 4 | TC-4.1a, TC-4.2b | `convex/packageSnapshots.test.ts` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:43:| Path 2.3 | Reopen the package later and keep pinned member versions stable even when newer artifact versions now exist | Story 4 | TC-4.3a, TC-4.3b | `tests/service/server/package-review-api.test.ts` |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-2.md:1:# Story 4 Fix Round 2\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-2.md:21:The Story 4 blocker is closed: current materials and outputs now have shipped durable writer paths plus direct Convex-layer verification, rather than depending only on seeded `InMemoryPlatformStore` state in service tests.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:3:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I’m starting by reading the required Story 4 artifacts in the order you gave, beginning with the Convex guidelines so the implementation stays aligned with project rules.\\\"}}\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:6:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I’ve loaded the Convex rules and I’m moving through the Story 4 artifacts now so I can isolate the two verified blockers without drifting into Story 5 or 6.\\\"}}\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-fix-round-1.jsonl:8:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/04-materials-and-outputs.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# Story 4: Materials and Outputs\\\\n\\\\n### Summary\\\\n<!-- Jira: Summary field -->\\\\nKeep the current artifacts, outputs, and source attachments visible so the user can follow what the process is working with right now.\\\\n\\\\n### Description\\\\n<!-- Jira: Description field -->\\\\n**User Profile**\\\\n\\\\n- **Primary User:** A technical founder, tech lead, staff engineer, or agentic operator who wants to run high-quality crafted processes through one durable project surface instead of manually stitching together prompts, tools, documents, and environments.\\\\n- **Context:** The user has opened a concrete process inside a project and needs to do the work of that process, not just manage shell-level summaries.\\\\n- **Mental Model:** \\\\\\\"I am inside one process. The process has a current phase, a running work history, current materials, and clear points where I need to respond, review, or let it continue.\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Key Constraint:** The work surface must support substantial process conversation and active progress without flattening the experience into generic chat or forcing the user to reconstruct context from the shell alone.\\\\n\\\\n**Objective**\\\\n\\\\nShow the current materials and outputs relevant to the active phase, keep identity and revision context clear, and define how materials-state replacements update the visible workspace when current process focus changes.\\\\n\\\\n**Scope**\\\\n\\\\nIn:\\\\n\\\\n- Show current artifacts, current outputs, and current source attachments alongside process work\\\\n- Make current identity and revision context visible for artifacts and outputs\\\\n- Replace visible materials state when phase, output revision, or focus changes\\\\n- Show a deliberate empty state when no current materials apply\\\\n\\\\nOut:\\\\n\\\\n- Detailed review rendering for materials and outputs\\\\n- Side-work summaries and attention-required state treatment\\\\n- WebSocket subscription lifecycle, reconnect, and degraded loading behavior\\\\n\\\\n**Dependencies**\\\\n\\\\n- Story 3 conversation/current-request slice\\\\n- Shared live-update vocabulary from Story 0 for fixture-applied `materials` snapshots and upserts\\\\n- Shared bootstrap/materials vocabulary from Story 0\\\\n- [tech-design.md](../tech-design.md), [tech-design-client.md](../tech-design-client.md), [tech-design-server.md](../tech-design-server.md)\\\\n- [test-plan.md](../test-plan.md)\\\\n\\\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\\\\n**AC-4.1:** The work surface keeps current phase-relevant artifacts, versions, source attachments, and current outputs visible alongside active process work.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.1a: Materials visible alongside process history**\\\\n  - Given: Process has current materials and outputs relevant to the active phase\\\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\\\n  - Then: The materials remain visible alongside the active process work rather than being hidden behind a separate later-only surface\\\\n- **TC-4.1b: Source attachments visible when relevant**\\\\n  - Given: Process is working from one or more attached sources\\\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\\\n  - Then: The relevant source attachments are visible with the process work\\\\n\\\\n**AC-4.2:** The visible materials make the current identity and revision context clear enough that the user can tell which artifact, version, source, or output the process is currently using or revising.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.2a: Current revision context visible for artifact**\\\\n  - Given: Process is using or revising an artifact with a current revision\\\\n  - When: The artifact appears in the work surface\\\\n  - Then: Its current identity and revision context are visible\\\\n- **TC-4.2b: Current output identity visible**\\\\n  - Given: Process has a current output in progress\\\\n  - When: The output appears in the work surface\\\\n  - Then: The user can tell which output the process is currently working on\\\\n\\\\n**AC-4.3:** When the process changes phase, revises an output, or switches focus, the visible materials update to match the current working context without requiring the user to infer the change from history alone.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.3a: Phase change updates visible materials**\\\\n  - Given: User is viewing a process work surface\\\\n  - When: The process advances into a new phase with different current materials\\\\n  - Then: The visible materials update to the new current set\\\\n- **TC-4.3b: Output revision updates visible context**\\\\n  - Given: Process revises an output while the user is viewing the work surface\\\\n  - When: The revision becomes current\\\\n  - Then: The visible output context updates to the new current revision\\\\n\\\\n**AC-4.4:** If no current materials or outputs are relevant to the active phase, the work surface shows a clear empty state instead of stale or carried-forward context.\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.4a: Empty materials state shown for phase with no current materials**\\\\n  - Given: Active process phase has no current materials or outputs to show\\\\n  - When: The work surface renders\\\\n  - Then: The materials area shows a clear empty state\\\\n- **TC-4.4b: Previous materials do not linger as current**\\\\n  - Given: Prior phase had visible materials but the current phase does not\\\\n  - When: The user enters the new phase\\\\n  - Then: The work surface does not keep showing the old materials as if they are still current\\\\n\\\\n### Technical Design\\\\n<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section ilable and revoked access states are safe |\\n| AC-6.3 | TC-6.3a | Story 6 | `tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts` | One failing source does not hide healthy sources |\\n\\n## Integration Path Trace\\n\\n| Path Segment | Description | Owning Story | Relevant TC | Verifying Test File(s) |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Path 1.1 | Attach a GitHub repository at project scope from the project shell | Story 1 | TC-1.1a, TC-1.2a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts` |\\n| Path 1.2 | Attach the same repository at process scope without colliding with the project-scoped source | Story 1 | TC-1.1b, TC-1.3c | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts` |\\n| Path 1.3 | Prevent an exact duplicate attach for the same scope and target ref | Story 1 | TC-1.3a, TC-1.3b | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`; `convex/sourceAttachments.test.ts` |\\n| Path 2.1 | Show source purpose, access mode, and target ref after attach | Story 2 | TC-2.1a, TC-2.3a, TC-2.3b | `tests/service/client/source-attachment-section.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/process-materials-section.test.ts` |\\n| Path 2.2 | Update target ref and mark a hydrated source stale | Story 2 | TC-2.2a, TC-2.4a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`; `convex/sourceAttachments.test.ts` |\\n| Path 3.1 | Render stale/not-hydrated/unavailable states with correct recovery affordances | Story 3 | TC-3.1a, TC-3.2a, TC-3.2b, TC-3.2c | `tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts` |\\n| Path 3.2 | Refresh one recoverable source and keep the rest of the list visible | Story 3 | TC-3.3a, TC-3.3b | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts` |\\n| Path 4.1 | Record and display sources that informed process work | Story 4 | TC-4.1a, TC-4.1b | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts` |\\n| Path 4.2 | Record and display writable source that received durable code updates while excluding read-only write targets | Story 4 | TC-4.2a, TC-4.3a | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts` |\\n| Path 4.3 | Degrade one provenance entry while keeping healthy provenance entries visible | Story 4 | TC-4.4a, TC-4.4b | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts` |\\n| Path 5.1 | Detach project-scoped and process-scoped sources from future current use | Story 5 | TC-5.1a, TC-5.1b | `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` |\\n| Path 5.2 | Detach during active process work without rewriting the hydrated working copy | Story 5 | TC-5.1c | `tests/service/server/process-execution-orchestrator.test.ts` |\\n| Path 5.3 | Preserve prior provenance and unrelated current sources after detach | Story 5 | TC-5.2a, TC-5.3a | `convex/sourceProvenance.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts` |\\n| Path 6.1 | Reopen project and process surfaces and restore durable source state | Story 6 | TC-6.1a, TC-6.1b | `tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts` |\\n| Path 6.2 | Show unavailable source safely or block revoked access without leaking source details | Story 6 | TC-6.2a, TC-6.2b | `tests/service/client/source-management-ui.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts` |\\n| Path 6.3 | Render healthy sources when one source independently fails | Story 6 | TC-6.3a | `tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts` |\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:309:| TC-6.1a | `tests/service/server/projects-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.1a reopens project source attachment state` | GET project shell returns source state after reload |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:310:| TC-6.1b | `tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts` | `TC-6.1b reopens process source attachment state` | GET process work surface returns current sources |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:342:| 6 Reopen/degraded | 5 | 0 | 5 | projects/process work surface API, UI |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:370:9. Reopen the project and process pages and confirm source/provenance state persists.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/01-attach-repositories-to-a-project-or-process/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:497:Caller implication: Read the public status and final package to decide impl-lead follow-up such as accept, reopen, or ruling.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state/progress/004-verify.progress.jsonl:2:{\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-04T23:15:18.582Z\",\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"phase\":\"verifier-initial\",\"event\":\"verifier-started\",\"summary\":\"Story verifier started for 06-reopen-and-degraded-source-state.\"}\ndocs/spec-b